---
// Shown on any method page whose frontmatter sets `firsthand: false`.
//
// The site's whole premise is field experience, so a page about a method the
// author has not personally used has to say so rather than borrow the
// credibility of the pages that are first-hand. Driven by the frontmatter flag,
// never hardcoded per page — scripts/audit/claims.mjs fails the build if a page
// with `firsthand: false` renders without this note.
---

<aside class="untested-note">
  <p class="untested-label">Not field-tested by me</p>
  <p class="untested-body">
    I haven't used this one myself. This page is based on the research and
    published guidance, not my own field experience.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .untested-note {
    background: #fffbeb;
    border: 1px solid #fcd34d;
    border-left: 4px solid #d4af37;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .untested-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #92400e;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

  .untested-body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #78350f;
  }
</style>
